# Beats — the Mods
#
# A beat plays in the binding scope of the hook that diverted to it, so
# `guest` and `self` are already bound here.

# Moderator_Prime greets a guest, gated on faction and accumulated trust.
== mod_scan(guest)
  cast: Moderator_Prime, guest

  MODERATOR_PRIME
    <if: guest.faction == Chatters>
      A Chatter. Behave, or you're getting banned.
      <set: Moderator_Prime.trusts.guest -= 10>
    <else>
      <if: Moderator_Prime.trusts.guest > 55>
        Always good to see a face I trust. Keep it up.
      <else>
        A fellow Mod. Good to see you.
        <set: guest.score += 50>
        <set: Moderator_Prime.trusts.guest += 10>
        <respond: Verified Mod — score {guest.score}, trust {Moderator_Prime.trusts.guest}.>

# Mod_Karen reports troublemakers. She can't lock anyone down — but
# leaning on a Chatter raises their heat, and the Algorithm reads heat.
== mod_report(guest)
  cast: Mod_Karen, guest
  MOD_KAREN
    <if: guest.faction == Chatters>
      I'm watching you, troublemaker. Keep it up and you'll be reported.
      <set: guest.heat += 30>
      <set: Mod_Karen.trusts.guest -= 5>
    <else if: guest.verified>
      A verified human. Carry on, citizen.
      <set: guest.karma += 5>
    <else>
      Keep it civil and we won't have a problem.
  # If she pushed them over the edge, the Algorithm — not Karen — acts.
  -> lockdown
